{"parentUuid":"098f0096-c76a-4ab5-ae2a-b08dd5de065d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01AKyNCabYJKeEBMo5LaWWgx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A **task checkpoint** is a checkpoint created from a subagent invocation rather than from a top-level user turn.\n\nWhen the main agent calls a sub-tool that spawns its own conversation (Claude Code's `Task` tool, OpenCode's subagent runs, etc.), the CLI saves a separate checkpoint scoped to that subagent run. They show up alongside session checkpoints in `entire explain` because rewinding to a task checkpoint is a useful unit (\"undo just what the subagent did\").\n\nTwo practical differences from a session checkpoint:\n- **No `SessionPrompt`** in most cases — the user didn't type anything; the parent agent dispatched the task with internal instructions, so there's nothing user-facing to show as the prompt.\n- **`IsTaskCheckpoint = true`** — flagged separately so the UI can label it `[Task]` and so commands like `entire rewind --task` can scope to subagent boundaries.\n\nThat's why the \"(no prompt)\" fallback matters most for these — they're the realistic case where there's no user prompt to display, and we want to surface *something* useful (the task description, the commit message, etc.) instead of an unhelpful `(no prompt)` placeholder.\n\nWant me to push a version that just compares α and γ (since β's special-casing of `[Task]` adds a code path you may not want), or are you ready to pick?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1031,"cache_read_input_tokens":112663,"output_tokens":449,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1031,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":449,"cache_read_input_tokens":112663,"cache