{"parentUuid":"2ca9ba0d-1cc4-426e-ad4a-9c70f0a91620","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e25bee25-45b3-44d6-8ebd-a0af7580eda4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fwaujtu3MT3Y6ZcpEtMMXZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Format `entire explain --generate` summary output\n2\t\n3\t**Status:** Draft\n4\t**Date:** 2026-04-29\n5\t**Branch:** `format-entire-explain`\n6\t\n7\t## Problem\n8\t\n9\t`entire explain --generate` (and `entire explain <ckpt>` when an AI summary already exists) prints a flat ASCII document to the terminal. Section headers (`Intent:`, `Outcome:`, `Learnings:`, `Friction:`, `Open Items:`) all share the same weight and color, so visual hierarchy is invisible. By contrast, `entire dispatch` renders LLM-generated markdown through `glamour` with a brand palette (orange H1, cyan H2, indigo H3, orange bullets/code) and reads as a polished engineering report.\n10\t\n11\tThe two commands produce conceptually similar artifacts — a curated summary of agent work — yet only dispatch looks the part.\n12\t\n13\t## Goal\n14\t\n15\tBring `entire explain` summary output up to dispatch's visual quality on TTY, without breaking pipe consumers, without growing new files, and without disturbing unrelated explain flows (`--short`, `--raw-transcript`, branch listing).\n16\t\n17\t## Non-goals\n18\t\n19\t- Reformatting the default `entire explain` branch listing (the no-args output produced by `runExplainBranchDefault`).\n20\t- A `--markdown` flag to force markdown in TTYs.\n21\t- Decomposing the 2410-line `explain.go` into subpackages.\n22\t- Token-display unification between `entire explain` and `entire status` beyond reusing the existing `formatTokenCount` helper.\n23\t- Markdown styling for `--short` output (intentionally terse).\n24\t\n25\t## Design summary\n26\t\n27\tWhen the writer is a real TTY (`shouldUseColor(w)` returns true) **and** `meta.Summary != nil`, `formatCheckpointOutput` builds a markdown document and renders it through `glamour` using the same brand styles dispatch uses. When piped, redirected, or `NO_COLOR=1`, it writes the same markdown text verbatim. The metadata header above the summary is hand-styled via lipgloss (column-aligned `key value` rows) — it doesn't go through `glamour`.\n28\t\n29\tNo new files. Two existing files change:\n30\t\n31\t- `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go` — `formatCheckpointOutput` gains a markdown branch; new helpers `buildSummaryMarkdown` and `formatCheckpointHeader` are added; `outputWithPager` injects `LESS=-R` when safe.\n32\t- `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_tui.go` — `dispatchMarkdownStyles` and `dispatchMarkdownStylesForBackground` are renamed to `entireBrandMarkdownStyles` and `entireBrandMarkdownStylesForBackground` so the explain caller doesn't read awkwardly. `defaultRenderTerminalMarkdown` keeps its name; explain calls it directly.\n33\t\n34\t## User-facing behavior\n35\t\n36\t### Output shape on TTY\n37\t\n38\t```\n39\t● Checkpoint a3b2c4d5e6f7\n40\t  session  2026-04-29-7f3c1a\n41\t  created  2026-04-29 14:22:08\n42\t  author   Peyton Montei <peyton@entire.io>\n43\t  tokens   18.4k\n44\t  commits  9f2c11a feat(auth): rotate session tokens on logout\n45\t\n46\t────────────────────────────────────────────\n47\t\n48\t## Intent\n49\t\n50\tRotate session tokens on every logout to invalidate stale cookies."}]},"uuid":"4c515505-9624-4b66-94eb-ee3a0a4541c4","timestamp":"2026-04-30T09:06:41.383Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/format-entire-explain/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-29-format-entire-explain-design.md","content":"# Format `entire explain --generate` summary output\n\n**Status:** Draft\n**Date:** 2026-04-29\n**Branch:** `format-entire-explain`\n\n## Problem\n\n`entire explain --generate` (and `entire explain <ckpt>` when an AI summary already exists) prints a flat ASCII document to the terminal. Section headers (`Intent:`, `Outcome:`, `Learnings:`, `Friction:`, `Open Items:`) all share the same weight and color, so visual hierarchy is invisible. By contrast, `entire dispatch` renders LLM-generated markdown through `glamour` with a brand palette (orange H1, cyan H2, indigo H3, orange bullets/code) and reads as a polished engineering report.\n\nThe two commands produce conceptually similar artifacts — a curated summary of agent work — yet only dispatch looks the part.\n\n## Goal\n\nBring `entire explain` summary output up to dispatch's visual quality on TTY, without breaking pipe consumers, without growing new files, and without disturbing unrelated explain flows (`--short`, `--raw-transcript`, branch listing).\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Reformatting the default `entire explain` branch listing (the no-args output produced by `runExplainBranchDefault`).\n- A `--markdown` flag to force markdown in TTYs.\n- Decomposing the 2410-line `explain.go` into subpackages.\n- Token-display unification between `entire explain` and `entire status` beyond reusing the existing `formatTokenCount` helper.\n- Markdown styling for `--short` output (intentionally terse).\n\n## Design summary\n\nWhen the writer is a real TTY (`shouldUseColor(w)` returns true) **and** `meta.Summary != nil`, `formatCheckpointOutput` builds a markdown document and renders it through `glamour` using the same brand styles dispatch uses. When piped, redirected, or `NO_COLOR=1`, it writes the same markdown text verbatim. The metadata header above the summary is hand-styled via lipgloss (column-aligned `key value` rows) — it doesn't go through `glamour`.\n\nNo new files. Two existing files change:\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go` — `formatCheckpointOutput` gains a markdown branch; new helpers `buildSummaryMarkdown` and `formatCheckpointHeader` are added; `outputWithPager` injects `LESS=-R` when safe.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_tui.go` — `dispatchMarkdownStyles` and `dispatchMarkdownStylesForBackground` are renamed to `entireBrandMarkdownStyles` and `entireBrandMarkdownStyles