{"parentUuid":"6d621cfd-10ec-4947-9ebc-6f6892870557","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_012GnxXwVtX3mhZKMWutH1Wb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N2VQ1B4SfhuwSirn3kpk6x","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/format-entire-explain/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-30-explain-unified-format-design.md","content":"# Unify `entire explain` output format across all surfaces\n\n**Status:** Draft\n**Date:** 2026-04-30\n**Branch:** `format-entire-explain`\n**Predecessor:** [`2026-04-29-format-entire-explain-design.md`](./2026-04-29-format-entire-explain-design.md) (PR #1078)\n\n## Problem\n\nPR #1078 brought the brand format to one path: a committed checkpoint with an AI summary present. Everything else `entire explain` can print still uses the old plain-text format and reads as a different command:\n\n| Surface | Today |\n| --- | --- |\n| **A.** Committed checkpoint, no AI summary | Styled header, then plain `Intent: <prompt>` / `Outcome: (not generated)` |\n| **B.** Temporary (uncommitted) checkpoint | No styled header at all — bare `Checkpoint: <sha> [temporary]` / `Session: ...` / `Intent: ...` / `Outcome: (not generated)` |\n| **C.** List view (`explain` no args) | `Branch: <name>` / `[cpID] [indicators] (no prompt)` / indented commits |\n| **D.** Session view (`explain --session <id>`) | `Session: ... / Strategy: ... / ─── Checkpoint N [...] ───` with raw `## Prompt` markdown not rendered |\n| **E.** Failure messages | Plain `fmt.Errorf` / `fmt.Fprintln` to stderr — no styling |\n| **F.** Generation success | One-line `✓ Summary generated and saved` plus plain `Provider: / Model:` lines |\n\nThe result is jarring: run `--generate` once and you get a polished card; run `explain` again before generating and you get the 1990s plain-text fallback. Failure messages don't share a shape with anything.\n\n## Goal\n\nOne brand-consistent shape across A–F. Same styled header, same metadata-row treatment, same brand markdown renderer for prose bodies, same fallback to plain text on `NO_COLOR` / piped output. The list view also gets the styled header treatment, and `(no prompt)` is replaced with a useful fallback.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Changing what data each surface shows (no new lookups, no extra round-trips).\n- Decomposing `explain.go` further than minor helper extraction.\n- A `--markdown` flag, a `--plain` flag, or any user-facing output toggle. Color/format follow `shouldUseColor(w)` like before.\n- Restyling raw transcripts (`--full`, `--verbose`, `--raw-transcript`) — they keep the existing `summarize.FormatCondensedTranscript` shape.\n- Any change to PR #1078's TTY-detected pager logic.\n- Any change to checkpoint storage, session phases, or hooks.\n\n## Design summary\n\nTwo existing helpers carry the visual identity today:\n\n1. `newStatusStyles(w)` in `status_style.go` — produces `colorEnabled`, `width`, and named styles (`dim`, `bold`, `green`, `red`, `yellow`, `agent`).\n2. `defaultRenderTerminalMarkdown(w, md)` in `dispatch_tui.go` — renders markdown through `glamour` with `entireBrandMarkdownStyles()`.\n\nThe unified design uses both across every surface, with three new tiny helpers on `statusStyles` to avoid duplicating the `● <label> <id>` / `✓ <label>` / `✗ <label>` shapes:\n\n```go\n// On statusStyles:\nfunc (s statusStyles) identityBullet(label, id string) string  // ● Checkpoint a3b2c4d5e6f7\nfunc (s statusStyles) successBullet(label string) string       // ✓ Summary generated\nfunc (s statusStyles) failureBullet(label string) string       // ✗ No associated Entire checkpoint\nfunc (s statusStyles) metadataRow(label, value string) string  // \"  session  2026-04-30-c4f1...\"\n```\n\nThese collapse to plain text when `colorEnabled` is false — no separate code path. `metadataRow` reuses the existing `%-9s` padding from `formatCheckpointHeader`'s closure (which is extracted to call this).\n\nBodies that today are plain key/value text (surfaces A, B, D) become markdown documents that route through `defaultRenderTerminalMarkdown`, matching the generated case. The shape is `## Intent` / `## Summary` / `## Files`, where `## Summary` is a one-paragraph italic affordance pointing at `--generate` when no AI summary exists.\n\nFailure messages (surface E) stop being thrown through `fmt.Errorf` for paths where we have a friendly version. Instead, the command prints the styled failure block to `cmd.ErrOrStderr()` and returns `NewSilentError(...)` so `main.go` doesn't double-print. This mirrors how `runExplain` already handles `paths.WorktreeRoot` errors per CLAUDE.md.\n\n## User-facing behavior\n\n### A. Committed checkpoint, no AI summary\n\n```\n● Checkpoint a3b2c4d5e6f7\n  session  2026-04-30-c4f1...\n  created  2026-04-30 14:22:00\n  author   Peyton Montei <peyton@entire.io>\n  tokens   1.2k\n  commits  e7f1a90 feat(cli): add --generate flag\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n## Intent\n\nadd explain --generate flag\n\n## Summary\n\n*Not generated yet. Run `entire explain --generate a3b2c4d5e6f7` to create an AI summary.*\n\n## Files (2)        [verbose/full only]\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/explain_test.go`\n```\n\n`## Intent` is `meta.Summary == nil` ? extracted prompt : `s.Intent`. The italic `## Summary` paragraph is the no-summary affordance. When `meta.Summary != nil`, the body is exactly today's PR #1078 output — no regression. The intent extraction logic moves to a single function (currently inlined in `formatCheckpointOutput`) so both paths share it.\n\n### B. Temporary (uncommitted) checkpoint\n\n```\n● Checkpoint 3f0aa11 [temporary]\n  session  2026-04-30-9c1f...\n  created  2026-04-30 13:58:14\n  author   Peyton Montei <peyton@entire.io>\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n## Intent\n\nrefactor explain header rendering\n\n## Summary\n\n*Not generated. Temporary checkpoints can be summarized after commit. Run `entire explain --generate` on the resulting commit.*\n```\n\nThe `[temporary]` indicator is dim, appended to the headline (mirrors how `[Task]` is treated in the list view). The metadata block omits `tokens` and `commits` because those don't apply to temporary checkpoints.\n\n### C. List view\n\n```\nBranch  format-entire-explain\n        3 checkpoints\n\n● a3b2c4d5e6f7  \"add explain --generate flag\"\n  04-30 14:22  e7f1a90  feat(cli): add --generate flag\n  04-30 14:18  b21c0fa  refactor(cli): split explain header\n\n● 9c1f2a3b4d5e  [Task]  refactor explain.go split\n  04-30 14:05  d11abcd  feat(cli): wire up paging\n\n● 3f0aa11      [temporary]  (no prompt recorded)\n  04-30 13:58  3f0aa11  Checkpoint: 9c1f2a3b4d5e\n```\n\nEach group gets the orange `●` + bold ID treatment. The `(no prompt)` fallback cascade (chosen during brainstorming, option α with the simplification that there is no special \"task vs non-task\" split):\n\n1. If `point.SessionPrompt != \"\"` → quoted prompt, truncated.\n2. Else if the group's latest commit message is non-empty → that message, no quotes (it's a commit subject, not a user utterance).\n3. Else → dim `(no prompt recorded)`.\n\nThe branch header becomes a small two-line block to match the `metadataRow` shape, dropping the `Filtered by session: ...` line into the same shape when `--session` is passed.\n\n### D. Session view\n\n```\n● Session 2026-04-30-c4f1...\n  strategy     manual-commit\n  started      2026-04-30 09:12:00\n  source ref   HEAD\n  checkpoints  3\n\n── Checkpoint 1  a3b2c4d5e6f7  2026-04-30 09:34 ────────────────\n\n## Prompt\n\nadd explain --generate flag\n\n## Files (2)\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/explain_test.go`\n\n── Checkpoint 2  9c1f2a3b4d5e  2026-04-30 11:08  [Task] ─────────\n\n## Prompt\n\n*(no prompt recorded)*\n```\n\n`formatSessionInfo` keeps its current responsibility (header + per-checkpoint blocks) but rewrites both pieces to use `statusStyles`. The `─── Checkpoint N [%s] ... ───` rule becomes a `sectionRule(...)` call. The `## Prompt` / `## Responses` markdown that already exists in `formatSessionInfo` is now actually rendered through `defaultRenderTerminalMarkdown` instead of being emitted as raw markdown.\n\n### E. Failures\n\nThree sub-shapes — same identity (red `✗` + bold label) with metadata rows beneath:\n\n**E1. No Entire-Checkpoint trailer** (replaces `printNoTrailerMessage`):\n\n```\n✗ No associated Entire checkpoint\n  commit  3f0aa11\n  reason  no Entire-Checkpoint trailer\n  hint    this commit was not created during an Entire session,\n          or the trailer was removed\n```\n\n**E2. Ambiguous checkpoint prefix** (replaces both the committed-side `errAmbiguousCommitPrefix` rendering in `resolveCommitUnambiguous` and the temporary-side ambiguous-prefix block in `explainTemporaryCheckpoint`):\n\n```\n✗ Ambiguous checkpoint prefix \"3f\"\n  matches  2 temporary checkpoints\n    • 3f0aa11  2026-04-30 13:58:14  session 2026-04-30-9c1f...\n    • 3f1c2d3  2026-04-30 14:02:01  session 2026-04-30-c4f1...\n  hint     use a longer prefix or a full SHA\n```\n\n**E3. Summary generation failed** (replaces the multi-line `formatCheckpointSummaryError` rendering for the deadline path; auth/rate-limit/config/CLI-missing keep their existing wording but get the bullet+rows wrapper):\n\n```\n✗ Summary generation timed out after 30s\n  causes\n    • the selected model is taking longer than expected on a large transcript\n    • the summary provider's CLI cannot reach its API (network, VPN, firewall)\n    • the provider's API is degraded\n  try     run the provider CLI directly to confirm it works\n```\n\nFor E1 and E2, the command prints to `cmd.ErrOrStderr()` and returns `NewSilentError(...)` so `main.go` doesn't double-print. For E3, the existing `formatCheckpointSummaryError` keeps building the same content but routes it through a new `renderFailure(w, label, rows)` helper; the `error` it returns is wrapped in `NewSilentError` at the call site in `runExplainCheckpoint`.\n\nOther failure surfaces that get the same wrapper:\n\n- `\"checkpoint X has no transcript\"` → `✗ Checkpoint has no transcript` + `id` row + hint.\n- `\"checkpoint X has no transcript content for this checkpoint (scoped)\"` → same shape, different hint.\n- `\"checkpoint X already has a summary (use --force to regenerate)\"` → `✗ Summary already exists` + `id` row + `try entire explain --generate --force <id>` hint.\n- `\"commit not found: <ref>\"` → `✗ Commit not found` + `ref` row.\n\n### F. Generation success\n\n```\n● Summary generated for a3b2c4d5e6f7\n  provider  claude-code\n  model     claude-sonnet-4-6\n  tokens    8.4k\n  duration  4.2s\n```\n\nThe orange `●` headline matches the `● Checkpoint <id>` family — generation success is conceptually \"here's the new state of this checkpoint.\" The `tokens` row reuses `formatTokenCount`. `duration` is the round of the value already returned by `generateCheckpointAISummary`.\n\n`formatSummaryProviderDetails` is renamed to a builder that returns `(label, []row)` so `renderSuccess` can format it consistently.\n\n## Architecture\n\n### File layout\n\nNo new files. Three files change:\n\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/status_style.go`** — adds `identityBullet`, `successBullet`, `failureBullet`, `metadataRow`, `renderSuccess`, `renderFailure`, `renderIdentity` helpers. These are method-on-`statusStyles` so they share the `colorEnabled` plumbing.\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/explain.go`** — rewrites bodies of `formatCheckpointOutput` (no-summary branch), `explainTemporaryCheckpoint`, `formatBranchCheckpoints`/`formatCheckpointGroup`, `formatSessionInfo`, `printNoTrailerMessage`. Extracts shared helpers: `extractIntent(prompts, content)`, `buildNoSummaryMarkdown(intent, files, hint)`, `renderExplainBody(w, md)` (handles the `shouldUseColor` branch + fallback). The ambiguous-prefix and no-trailer error renderers move to a small `failures.go`-style block at the bottom of `explain.go` (no new file).\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/explain_summary_provider.go`** — replaces `formatSummaryProviderDetails(provider) string` with `summaryProviderRows(provider) []row` (or equivalent). Callers join via `renderSuccess`.\n\n### Data flow\n\nSame as today. Each surface already has the data it needs:\n\n- A: `meta.Summary`, `meta.FilesTouched`, scoped prompt extraction, `author`, `tokenUsage`, `associatedCommits` — all already passed to `formatCheckpointOutput`.\n- B: `tc.SessionID`, `tc.Timestamp`, shadow tree's `prompt.txt` — already loaded.\n- C: `[]strategy.RewindPoint` — already grouped by `groupByCheckpointID`.\n- D: `*strategy.Session` and `[]checkpointDetail` — already built upstream.\n- E: every error path already has the values it needs (commit hash, prefix, deadline, etc.).\n- F: provider info + duration are already returned by `generateCheckpointAISummary`.\n\nThe change is exclusively in how that data gets emitted.\n\n### Color / NO_COLOR / piped behavior\n\nSame rule as today: `shouldUseColor(w)` decides per-call. When false:\n\n- `identityBullet`/`successBullet`/`failureBullet` emit `● Checkpoint a3b2c4d5e6f7` / `✓ Summary generated` / `✗ ...` with the same glyph but no ANSI escapes.\n- `metadataRow` emits `  session  <value>` — same padding, no dim.\n- `renderExplainBody` emits the markdown source verbatim instead of running `glamour`.\n- The horizontal rule and section rules emit raw `─` characters at the same width.\n\nThis is the existing pattern — every helper already branches on `colorEnabled`.\n\n### Error handling\n\nThe dual-write pattern (print styled to stderr, return `NewSilentError`) requires that:\n\n1. `runExplainCheckpoint` and `runExplainCommit` get an `errW io.Writer` parameter (already have one — `errW`). Verified at line 332 + 481 + 2045.\n2. `runExplain` propagates `cmd.ErrOrStderr()` into those calls. Already does.\n3. `cmd.SilenceUsage = true` for the styled-failure paths so cobra doesn't append usage text after our nicely formatted error block.\n\nFailures we leave alone (still raw `fmt.Errorf`):\n\n- \"failed to write transcript: %v\" — internal I/O failure, no useful structured message.\n- Anything wrapped from go-git (`failed to get HEAD: %w`, etc.) — internal, not actionable.\n\n## Components\n\n```\n┌─ status_style.go ───────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  identityBullet(label, id) string                           │\n│  successBullet(label) string                                │\n│  failureBullet(label) string                                │\n│  metadataRow(label, value string) string                    │\n│  metadataRows(rows []row) string                            │\n│  renderIdentity(w, label, id, rows) — bullet + rows + rule  │\n│  renderSuccess(w, label, rows)                              │\n│  renderFailure(w, label, rows)                              │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │\n                           │ used by\n                           ▼\n┌─ explain.go ────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  formatCheckpointOutput      — A (no-summary branch only)   │\n│  explainTemporaryCheckpoint  — B                            │\n│  formatBranchCheckpoints     — C                            │\n│  formatCheckpointGroup       — C                            │\n│  formatSessionInfo           — D                            │\n│  printNoTrailerMessage       — E1                           │\n│  resolveCommitUnambiguous    — E2 (ambiguous commit)        │\n│  explainTemporaryCheckpoint  — E2 (ambiguous shadow prefix) │\n│  formatCheckpointSummaryError — E3 (deadline + auth/rate/…) │\n│  generateCheckpointSummary   — F                            │\n│  buildNoSummaryMarkdown      — new shared helper for A+B    │\n│  extractIntent               — new shared helper for A+B    │\n│  renderExplainBody           — new shared helper            │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n## Testing\n\nThe test surface is large but mostly mechanical — `explain_test.go` is already 600+ lines of golden assertions on output strings. The plan:\n\n1. **Update existing assertions**. Every `assert.Contains(out, \"Outcome: (not generated)\")` becomes `assert.Contains(out, \"## Summary\")`. Every `assert.Contains(out, \"(no prompt)\")` becomes `assert.Contains(out, \"(no prompt recorded)\")`. Every `assert.Contains(out, \"No associated Entire checkpoint\\n\")` becomes the new failure-bullet shape.\n2. **Add NO_COLOR cases** for each surface. PR #1078 already added one — extend the table to cover A, B, C, D, E1, E2, E3, F.\n3. **Add a \"no double-print\" test** for E1+E2: stub `cmd.ErrOrStderr()` to a buffer, run, assert the styled failure appears exactly once and the returned error is `*SilentError`.\n4. **Add an \"intent fallback\" test** for A: when `content.Prompts == \"\"` and `scopedPrompts == nil`, the markdown body still renders without panic and `## Intent` shows `(no prompt recorded)`.\n5. **Vogon canary**. The Vogon binary parses prompts via regex; this PR doesn't change any prompt text, so canary should pass without binary changes. Verified by `mise run test:e2e:canary` post-implementation per CLAUDE.md.\n6. **`mise run check`** — formats, lints, runs unit + integration + canary.\n\nExisting tests covered by PR #1078 (`TestFormatCheckpointOutput_*`) form the regression baseline for surface A's generated-summary path; that path doesn't change.\n\n## Risks\n\n- **Test churn**. `explain_test.go` has many `assert.Contains` on plain strings — every surface in scope likely has an assertion that needs updating. Mitigation: do the test sweep in the same PR as the implementation, not as follow-up.\n- **Output stability for scripts**. `entire explain` output is consumed by humans, but it's possible some users grep it. The `Cursor Bugbot` review on PR #1078 already flagged \"moderate compatibility risk for scripts/tests that parse explain output.\" Mitigation: the structural keys (`Intent`, `Summary`, `Files`, the checkpoint ID, the commit SHAs) are all preserved or upgraded to markdown headings — anyone grepping `Intent:` was already broken by PR #1078.\n- **Pager interaction with `✗` bullets**. The pager already handles styled output correctly (PR #1078's `LESS=-R` work). No new risk.\n- **Glamour rendering of italic affordance**. `*Not generated yet…*` rendered through `glamour` with the brand styles is currently un-tested. Mitigation: add a dedicated TTY snapshot test that confirms the italic block renders without breaking the surrounding metadata block.\n- **Subagent test-doubling**. The `formatSummaryProviderDetails` rename to `summaryProviderRows` is consumed only by `generateCheckpointSummary` per grep. Verified single call site.\n\n## Out-of-scope follow-ups\n\n- A `--format=json` flag for scripted consumers (separate work).\n- Decomposing `explain.go` into `explain/` subpackages — file is now 2546 lines; this PR adds maybe 40-50 net lines and isn't the right time to split.\n- Aligning `entire status`'s identity-bullet shape with the new `identityBullet` helper (currently uses its own ad-hoc render path; could DRY in a follow-up but doesn't block this work).\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- All six surfaces (A–F) emit the brand-shaped output on TTY and identical text-mode output under `NO_COLOR=1` / piping, verified by tests.\n- `(no prompt)` is replaced by the option-α cascade (prompt → commit subject → `(no prompt recorded)`).\n- No surface still uses unwrapped `fmt.Errorf` for the patterns listed in §E (no-trailer, ambiguous, summary errors, no transcript, already exists).\n- `mise run check` passes; `mise run test:e2e:canary` passes.\n- Diff stays within `explain.go`, `status_style.go`, `explain_summary_provider.go`, plus their tests. No new files.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":