{"parentUuid":"7badaee8-4f6d-4c94-863b-972ff7f68db2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"416f3ea9-e87e-4d4a-8bba-f75cbeda97ba","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UZawhsGaPAvMxiwFKHCmun","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/format-entire-explain/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-30-explain-unified-format.md"}]},"uuid":"8ed4495f-f8a2-421f-9de1-eab712331224","timestamp":"2026-04-30T09:51:36.305Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/format-entire-explain/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-30-explain-unified-format.md","content":"# Unified `entire explain` output format — Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Bring the brand-shaped output format introduced by PR #1078 to every other surface of `entire explain` (no-summary, temporary, list, session, failures, success), and replace the unhelpful `(no prompt)` fallback with a useful cascade.\n\n**Architecture:** Add a small set of package-private helpers on `statusStyles` (identity / success / failure bullets, metadata rows, render wrappers) plus a single body renderer that routes through `defaultRenderTerminalMarkdown`. Each `entire explain` output path is rewritten to call those helpers; no new files. Failure paths write the styled block to `errW` and return `*SilentError` so `main.go` doesn't double-print.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26, lipgloss, glamour (existing brand renderer in `dispatch_tui.go`), cobra. No new dependencies.\n\n**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-30-explain-unified-format-design.md`\n\n**Pre-flight:**\n- This plan executes inside the existing worktree `format-entire-explain`. The branch already contains PR #1078's changes (e008cc705 merged from origin/main).\n- Per user preference, design/plan docs in `docs/superpowers/` are **not** committed.\n- Code commits in this plan should be made (the no-commit rule applies only to planning docs under `docs/superpowers/`).\n- Every code commit message must end with the `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>` trailer (per CLAUDE.md commit conventions).\n\n**Verification before any push:** `mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci`. The full canary (`mise run test:e2e:canary`) is part of `test:ci`. Do **not** run `mise run test:e2e` — those are real-API tests that cost money.\n\n---\n\n## File Structure\n\n| File | Change | Responsibility |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/status_style.go` | Modify | Add `explainRow` type + `identityBullet`, `successBullet`, `failureBullet`, `metadataRow`, `metadataRows`, `renderIdentity`, `renderSuccess`, `renderFailure` methods. ~80 net lines. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/status_style_test.go` | Modify | Unit tests for each new helper (color + NO_COLOR cases). |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go` | Modify | Add `extractIntent`, `buildNoSummaryMarkdown`, `renderExplainBody` helpers. Rewrite no-summary branch of `formatCheckpointOutput`, body of `explainTemporaryCheckpoint`, `formatBranchCheckpoints`, `formatCheckpointGroup`, `formatSessionInfo`, `printNoTrailerMessage`, ambiguous-prefix rendering. Refactor `formatCheckpointSummaryError` to return `(label, rows, error)`. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/explain_test.go` | Modify | Update existing assertions (`Outcome:`, `Strategy:`, `Source Ref:`, `(no prompt)`, `No associated Entire checkpoint\\n`). Add NO_COLOR cases per surface. Add intent-fallback test. Add no-double-print test. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/explain_summary_provider.go` | Modify | Replace `formatSummaryProviderDetails(p) string` with `summaryProviderRows(p) []explainRow`. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/explain_summary_provider_test.go` | Modify | Update assertions for new return shape. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/explain_test.go` | Modify | Update `\"No associated Entire checkpoint\"` assertion(s) to new failure shape. |\n| `e2e/tests/explain_test.go` | Audit | Confirm no legacy substrings; PR #1078 already updated this file. |\n\nNo new files. No new packages. No exported API surface changes outside this package.\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 1: Foundation helpers in `status_style.go`\n\nAdds the package-private types and methods every surface depends on. Verified in isolation before any explain.go changes.\n\n### Task 1.1: Add `explainRow` type and `metadataRow` / `metadataRows`\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/status_style.go` (add below `formatTokenCount`, before `horizontalRule`)\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/status_style_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**\n\nAppend to `status_style_test.go`:\n\n```go\nfunc TestMetadataRow_PadsLabelToMin9(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\ts := newStatusStyles(io.Discard) // colorEnabled=false, deterministic\n\tgot := s.metadataRow(\"session\", \"2026-04-30-c4f1\")\n\twant := \"  session    2026-04-30-c4f1\\n\"\n\tif got != want {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"metadataRow short-label padding\\n got: %q\\nwant: %q\", got, want)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestMetadataRow_PadsLongerLabelsByItself(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\ts := newStatusStyles(io.Discard)\n\tgot := s.metadataRow(\"checkpoints\", \"3\")\n\t// 11-char label, single space separator before value\n\twant := \"  checkpoints  3\\n\"\n\tif got != want {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"metadataRow long-label\\n got: %q\\nwant: %q\", got, want)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestMetadataRows_AlignsToWidestLabel(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\ts := newStatusStyles(io.Discard)\n\trows := []explainRow{\n\t\t{Label: \"session\", Value: \"abc\"},\n\t\t{Label: \"checkpoints\", Value: \"3\"},\n\t}\n\tgot := s.metadataRows(rows)\n\twant := \"  session      abc\\n  checkpoints  3\\n\"\n\tif got != want {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"metadataRows alignment\\n got: %q\\nwant: %q\", got, want)\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nThe `metadataRow` single-row form pads to a fixed minimum of 9 chars (matches today's closure in `formatCheckpointHeader`). The `metadataRows` plural form computes the max label width across the slice and uses `max(9, widest)` as the pad target so multi-row blocks align as a unit.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run tests to verify they fail**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/ -run 'TestMetadataRow|TestMetadataRows' -v`\nExpected: FAIL — `explainRow` undefined / `metadataRow` not a method.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement**\n\nIn `status_style.go`, add immediately above `horizontalRule`:\n\n```go\n// explainRow is one entry in a metadata block: dim label + plain value.\ntype explainRow struct {\n\tLabel string\n\tValue string\n}\n\n// metadataRow renders a single key/value row using a 9-char min-padded label.\n// Use metadataRows for multi-row blocks where alignment depends on the widest label.\nfunc (s statusStyles) metadataRow(label, value string) string {\n\treturn s.metadataRowsWithWidth([]explainRow{{Label: label, Value: value}}, 9)\n}\n\n// metadataRows joins rows with consistent label-column width: max(9, widest label) + 2-space gutter.\nfunc (s statusStyles) metadataRows(rows []explainRow) string {\n\twidth := 9\n\tfor _, r := range rows {\n\t\tif l := len(r.Label); l > width {\n\t\t\twidth = l\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn s.metadataRowsWithWidth(rows, width)\n}\n\nfunc (s statusStyles) metadataRowsWithWidth(rows []explainRow, width int) string {\n\tvar b strings.Builder\n\tfor _, r := range rows {\n\t\tpaddedLabel := fmt.Sprintf(\"%-*s\", width, r.Label)\n\t\tif s.colorEnabled {\n\t\t\tpaddedLabel = s.render(s.dim, paddedLabel)\n\t\t}\n\t\t// Two-space indent + padded label + two-space gutter + value + newline.\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(&b, \"  %s  %s\\n\", paddedLabel, r.Value)\n\t}\n\treturn b.String()\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Run tests to verify they pass**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/ -run 'TestMetadataRow|TestMetadataRows' -v`\nExpected: PASS (3/3).\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/status_style.go cmd/entire/cli/status_style_test.go\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfeat(cli): add explainRow type and metadataRow helpers\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 1.2: Add identity/success/failure bullets\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/status_style.go` (add above `metadataRow`)\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/status_style_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing tests**\n\n```go\nfunc TestIdentityBullet_NoColor(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\ts := newStatusStyles(io.Discard)\n\tgot := s.identityBullet(\"Checkpoint\", \"a3b2c4d5e6f7\")\n\twant := \"● Checkpoint a3b2c4d5e6f7\\n\"\n\tif got != want {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"identityBullet no-color\\n got: %q\\nwant: %q\", got, want)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestSuccessBullet_NoColor(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\ts := newStatusStyles(io.Discard)\n\tgot := s.successBullet(\"Summary generated\")\n\twant := \"✓ Summary generated\\n\"\n\tif got != want {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"successBullet no-color\\n got: %q\\nwant: %q\", got, want)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestFailureBullet_NoColor(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\ts := newStatusStyles(io.Discard)\n\tgot := s.failureBullet(\"No associated Entire checkpoint\")\n\twant := \"✗ No associated Entire checkpoint\\n\"\n\tif got != want {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"failureBullet no-color\\n got: %q\\nwant: %q\", got, want)\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run tests to verify they fail**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/ -run 'TestIdentityBullet|TestSuccessBullet|TestFailureBullet' -v`\nExpected: FAIL.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement**\n\nIn `status_style.go`, above `metadataRow`:\n\n```go\n// identityBullet renders \"● <label> <id>\\n\". Bullet is brand orange when color\n// is enabled; ID is also orange to mirror the existing checkpoint header.\nfunc (s statusStyles) identityBullet(label, id string) string {\n\tif !s.colorEnabled {\n\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"● %s %s\\n\", label, id)\n\t}\n\tbullet := s.render(lipgloss.NewStyle().Foreground(lipgloss.Color(\"#fb923c\")), \"●\")\n\tidStyled := s.render(lipgloss.NewStyle().Foreground(lipgloss.Color(\"#fb923c\")), id)\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s %s %s\\n\", bullet, s.render(s.bold, label), idStyled)\n}\n\n// successBullet renders \"✓ <label>\\n\" — green checkmark + bold label.\nfunc (s statusStyles) successBullet(label string) string {\n\tif !s.colorEnabled {\n\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"✓ %s\\n\", label)\n\t}\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s %s\\n\", s.render(s.green, \"✓\"), s.render(s.bold, label))\n}\n\n// failureBullet renders \"✗ <label>\\n\" — red ✗ + bold label.\nfunc (s statusStyles) failureBullet(label string) string {\n\tif !s.colorEnabled {\n\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"✗ %s\\n\", label)\n\t}\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s %s\\n\", s.render(s.red, \"✗\"), s.render(s.bold, label))\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Run tests to verify they pass**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/ -run 'TestIdentityBullet|TestSuccessBullet|TestFailureBullet' -v`\nExpected: PASS (3/3).\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/status_style.go cmd/entire/cli/status_style_test.go\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfeat(cli): add identity/success/failure bullet helpers\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 1.3: Add `renderIdentity`, `renderSuccess`, `renderFailure`\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/status_style.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/status_style_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing tests**\n\n```go\nfunc TestRenderIdentity_BulletRowsRule(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\ts := newStatusStyles(io.Discard)\n\tgot := s.renderIdentity(\"Checkpoint\", \"abc123\",\n\t\t[]explainRow{{Label: \"session\", Value: \"s1\"}, {Label: \"tokens\", Value: \"1.2k\"}},\n\t)\n\t// Expected layout: bullet line, two metadata rows, horizontal rule, trailing newline.\n\tif !strings.HasPrefix(got, \"● Checkpoint abc123\\n\") {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"missing identity bullet header in:\\n%s\", got)\n\t}\n\tif !strings.Contains(got, \"  session  s1\\n\") {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"missing session row in:\\n%s\", got)\n\t}\n\tif !strings.Contains(got, \"  tokens   1.2k\\n\") {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"missing tokens row in:\\n%s\", got)\n\t}\n\tif !strings.Contains(got, strings.Repeat(\"─\", 4)) {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"missing horizontal rule in:\\n%s\", got)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestRenderSuccess_BulletThenRows(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\ts := newStatusStyles(io.Discard)\n\tgot := s.renderSuccess(\"Summary generated for abc\",\n\t\t[]explainRow{{Label: \"provider\", Value: \"claude-code\"}},\n\t)\n\twant := \"✓ Summary generated for abc\\n  provider  claude-code\\n\"\n\tif got != want {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"renderSuccess\\n got: %q\\nwant: %q\", got, want)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestRenderFailure_BulletThenRows(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\ts := newStatusStyles(io.Discard)\n\tgot := s.renderFailure(\"Commit not found\",\n\t\t[]explainRow{{Label: \"ref\", Value: \"deadbeef\"}},\n\t)\n\twant := \"✗ Commit not found\\n  ref  deadbeef\\n\"\n\tif got != want {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"renderFailure\\n got: %q\\nwant: %q\", got, want)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestRenderFailure_NoRows(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\ts := newStatusStyles(io.Discard)\n\tgot := s.renderFailure(\"Operation failed\", nil)\n\twant := \"✗ Operation failed\\n\"\n\tif got != want {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"renderFailure no-rows\\n got: %q\\nwant: %q\", got, want)\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run tests to verify they fail**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/ -run 'TestRenderIdentity|TestRenderSuccess|TestRenderFailure' -v`\nExpected: FAIL.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement**\n\nIn `status_style.go`, below `failureBullet`:\n\n```go\n// renderIdentity returns identityBullet + metadataRows + horizontalRule + trailing newline.\n// This is the exact shape used by formatCheckpointHeader; rendering an entire\n// header block is one call instead of three.\nfunc (s statusStyles) renderIdentity(label, id string, rows []explainRow) string {\n\tvar b strings.Builder\n\tb.WriteString(s.identityBullet(label, id))\n\tb.WriteString(s.metadataRows(rows))\n\tb.WriteString(s.horizontalRule(s.width))\n\tb.WriteString(\"\\n\")\n\treturn b.String()\n}\n\n// renderSuccess returns successBullet + metadataRows. No trailing rule (success\n// blocks are short and don't precede a body section).\nfunc (s statusStyles) renderSuccess(label string, rows []explainRow) string {\n\tif len(rows) == 0 {\n\t\treturn s.successBullet(label)\n\t}\n\treturn s.successBullet(label) + s.metadataRows(rows)\n}\n\n// renderFailure returns failureBullet + metadataRows. Used when a command\n// prints a styled error block to errW before returning *SilentError.\nfunc (s statusStyles) renderFailure(label string, rows []explainRow) string {\n\tif len(rows) == 0 {\n\t\treturn s.failureBullet(label)\n\t}\n\treturn s.failureBullet(label) + s.metadataRows(rows)\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Run tests to verify they pass**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/ -run 'TestRenderIdentity|TestRenderSuccess|TestRenderFailure' -v`\nExpected: PASS (4/4).\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Run full status_style tests**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/ -run TestStatusStyle -v`\nExpected: PASS — verifies no regression in existing helpers.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/status_style.go cmd/entire/cli/status_style_test.go\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfeat(cli): add renderIdentity/renderSuccess/renderFailure composers\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 2: Body helpers in `explain.go`\n\nThree small functions that A, B, and D will all share. Built and tested before any surface is touched.\n\n### Task 2.1: Add `extractIntent`\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go` (above `formatCheckpointOutput`)\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/explain_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**\n\n```go\nfunc TestExtractIntent_PrefersScopedPrompt(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\tgot := extractIntent([]string{\"add explain --generate flag\", \"later prompt\"}, \"fallback prompt\\nline2\")\n\twant := \"add explain --generate flag\"\n\tif got != want {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"extractIntent scoped\\n got: %q\\nwant: %q\", got, want)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestExtractIntent_FallsBackToFirstLineOfContent(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\tgot := extractIntent(nil, \"first content line\\nsecond line\")\n\twant := \"first content line\"\n\tif got != want {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"extractIntent fallback\\n got: %q\\nwant: %q\", got, want)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestExtractIntent_EmptyReturnsEmpty(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\tif got := extractIntent(nil, \"\"); got != \"\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"extractIntent empty: got %q want empty\", got)\n\t}\n\tif got := extractIntent([]string{\"\"}, \"\"); got != \"\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"extractIntent empty-string-prompt: got %q want empty\", got)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestExtractIntent_TruncatesLongPrompts(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\tlong := strings.Repeat(\"a\", 500)\n\tgot := extractIntent([]string{long}, \"\")\n\tif len(got) >= len(long) {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected truncation; got %d chars\", len(got))\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run tests to verify they fail**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/ -run TestExtractIntent -v`\nExpected: FAIL — undefined `extractIntent`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement**\n\nIn `explain.go`, above `formatCheckpointOutput`:\n\n```go\n// extractIntent picks the user-facing intent line from available prompt sources.\n// Preference: first non-empty entry of scopedPrompts, then first non-empty line\n// of fallbackPrompts, then \"\". Truncates to maxIntentDisplayLength.\nfunc extractIntent(scopedPrompts []string, fallbackPrompts string) string {\n\tfor _, p := range scopedPrompts {\n\t\tif p == \"\" {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn strategy.TruncateDescription(p, maxIntentDisplayLength)\n\t}\n\tfor _, line := range strings.Split(fallbackPrompts, \"\\n\") {\n\t\tif line == \"\" {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn strategy.TruncateDescription(line, maxIntentDisplayLength)\n\t}\n\treturn \"\"\n}\n```\n\nThen **remove** the equivalent inlined logic from `formatCheckpointOutput` (lines 1357–1364) and from `explainTemporaryCheckpoint` (lines 1140–1145) — they will be replaced in Chunks 3 and 4. For now leave call sites referring to the existing local `intent` so nothing breaks.\n\nDefensive: do NOT change the call sites yet. This task only adds and tests the helper.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Run tests to verify they pass**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/ -run TestExtractIntent -v`\nExpected: PASS (4/4).\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/explain.go cmd/entire/cli/explain_test.go\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfeat(cli): add extractIntent helper for prompt-source cascade\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 2.2: Add `buildNoSummaryMarkdown`\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go` (alongside `buildSummaryMarkdown`)\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/explain_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**\n\n```go\nfunc TestBuildNoSummaryMarkdown_IntentAndAffordance(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\tgot := buildNoSummaryMarkdown(\"add explain --generate flag\", nil, \"Run `entire explain --generate abc`.\")\n\tif !strings.Contains(got, \"## Intent\\n\\nadd explain --generate flag\\n\") {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"missing intent section:\\n%s\", got)\n\t}\n\tif !strings.Contains(got, \"## Summary\\n\\n*Run `entire explain --generate abc`.*\\n\") {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"missing italic summary affordance:\\n%s\", got)\n\t}\n\tif strings.Contains(got, \"## Files\") {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"did not expect Files when files=nil:\\n%s\", got)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestBuildNoSummaryMarkdown_RendersFilesWhenProvided(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\tgot := buildNoSummaryMarkdown(\"intent\", []string{\"a.go\", \"b.go\"}, \"hint\")\n\tif !strings.Contains(got, \"